/-!
# `Work.MotAS.bwASpoly_fractionRing`

The chart denominator `bwASpoly a b g = bwASQ a b g + bwASR a b g` of the characteristic-`5`
(Artin–Schreier) Crauder–Katz chart cuts out a *rational* surface: its projective closure
`W·bwASQ + bwASR = 0 ⊆ ℙ³` is linear in `W`, hence birational to `ℙ²`, so

`FractionRing (K[X₀,X₁,X₂]/(bwASpoly a b g)) ≃ₐ[K] K(U)(V) = RatFunc (RatFunc K)`.

## Strategy (the "graph" parametrisation `thetaAS`)

Write `p := bwASpoly a b g = Q + R`, `Q := bwASQ a b g` (homogeneous of degree `2`),
`R := bwASR a b g` (homogeneous of degree `3`), and let

* `bwASQ2 = γV² − d²U − 2ed` and `bwASR2 = γU²V − edUV − 2edV³ + γV − gd²` be the dehomogenisations
  of `Q` and `R` at `X₂ = 1` (`Q̃`, `R̃` for their images in `Frac K[U,V]`),
* `thetaAS a b g : K[X₀,X₁,X₂] →ₐ[K] Frac K[U,V]` be the **graph parametrisation**
  `X₀ ↦ −U·Q̃/R̃`, `X₁ ↦ −V·Q̃/R̃`, `X₂ ↦ −Q̃/R̃`.

Then

1. (`§2`) `thetaAS` kills `p`: by the dehomogenisation identities `Q(x) = x₂²·Q̃(x₀/x₂, x₁/x₂)`,
   `R(x) = x₂³·R̃(x₀/x₂, x₁/x₂)` and `θ(x₀) = U·θ(x₂)`, `θ(x₁) = V·θ(x₂)`, one gets
   `θ(p) = θ(x₂)²·(Q̃ + θ(x₂)·R̃) = θ(x₂)²·(Q̃ − Q̃) = 0`.
2. (`§3`) The fraction field of `θ.range` is `K(U,V)`: since `U = θ(x₀)/θ(x₂)` and
   `V = θ(x₁)/θ(x₂)`, the subfield generated by `θ.range` in `Frac K[U,V]` contains `U`, `V`, hence
   is everything.
3. (`§4`) `trdeg K (Frac (K[X]/(ker θ))) = trdeg K (Frac (θ.range)) = trdeg K K(U,V) = 2`, so by
   `height_eq_one_of_trdeg_eq_two` the prime `ker θ` has height `1`.
4. (`§5`) `(p) ⊆ ker θ` and both are height-one primes (Krull for `(p)`), so `(p) = ker θ`.
5. (`§6`) Assembly: `Frac (K[X]/(p)) = Frac (K[X]/(ker θ)) ≃ₐ[K] Frac (θ.range) ≃ₐ[K] K(U,V) ≃ₐ[K]
   RatFunc (RatFunc K)`.

This avoids having to prove anything about the *rationality of the surface directly*: the
parametrisation `thetaAS` is the graph of the ratio `−R/Q`, and the two-dimensionality of the
residue field comes for free from `U`, `V`.
-/

